  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>∆</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∆</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>S</mi></math><br /><br />Where, <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Gibbs free energy change<br /><br /><math><mo>∆</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Enthalpy change<br /><br /><math><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Temperature in k and <br /><br /><math><mo>∆</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Entropy change<br /><br />A reaction is spontaneous, when <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>G</mi></math> is negative. If <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>S</mi></math> is positive, <math><mi>T</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>S</mi></math> become positive, so that <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>S</mi></math> can become negative.",
